# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Volley Ball Game project following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Created package.json
- **File**: `Volley Ball Game/package.json`
- **Purpose**: Added dependency management for the project
- **Content**: Configured project metadata and added `@vercel/speed-insights` as a dependency

### 2. Installed Dependencies
- **Package**: `@vercel/speed-insights` (version 1.3.1)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Lockfile**: Created `package-lock.json` for consistent dependency resolution

### 3. Modified index.html
- **File**: `Volley Ball Game/index.html`
- **Changes**: Added Vercel Speed Insights scripts to the `<head>` section
- **Implementation**: Following the vanilla JS/HTML pattern from official Vercel documentation
  - Added Speed Insights initialization script: `window.si = window.si || function () { ... }`
  - Added deferred Speed Insights loader: `<script defer src="/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js"></script>`
- **Location**: Placed immediately after the existing Vercel Web Analytics scripts for consistency

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- **Project Type**: Vanilla HTML/JavaScript with Three.js
- **Pattern Used**: Vanilla JS implementation (as per Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide)

### Installation Method
The installation followed the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide:
1. Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
2. Identified the project as a vanilla HTML/JS project
3. Applied the vanilla JS pattern with deferred script loading
4. Scripts will be served from `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` after deployment

### Testing & Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
- ✅ Dependencies installed without vulnerabilities
- ✅ package-lock.json generated for dependency locking
- ✅ HTML structure preserved and validated
- ✅ Speed Insights scripts added in correct location

## Next Steps

After deploying to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Navigate to Project Settings → Speed Insights
3. Click "Enable" to activate the feature
4. Performance metrics will be available in the dashboard after users visit the site

## Notes

- The Speed Insights scripts follow the same pattern as the existing Vercel Web Analytics implementation
- Scripts are loaded with `defer` attribute for optimal performance
- No changes to existing functionality - only additive changes made
- The project structure and existing code remain completely intact
- Speed Insights will automatically track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP)
